# The edge of what a-birth-that-moves-down-to-where-a-copy-leaves-is-no-deed-in-the-net-of-effects.ir lets by. The literal is born in front of the copy of bump(), and the copy stores into it: that store is seen if
# it runs again. The walk knows, so no copy leaves for the call behind it. UnderstateEffects:RestartMark/all/RunsOtherCode lays the mark false: as built bump() then runs twice on one cell, in silence; under the net
# the store is counted, though it fills a cell that its own unit has made, because the beginning of what may run again stands between the birth and the store. f5 = the first arrow
